<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{EB0EE517-2E19-519B-22E0-A806D21D10E9}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="43" name="Text Placeholder 42"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{1A581C05-1BD2-2572-6FCA-9B9B484C9BBF}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="62"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" dirty="0"/><a:t> </a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="21" name="Text Placeholder 20"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{7DB76C99-7E31-52EE-A479-148B79FA32F4}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="body" idx="33"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr/><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" sz="1200" b="1" dirty="0"/><a:t>Harness automation to bolster convenience. </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" sz="1200" dirty="0"/><a:t>Consider how you can use automation to offer on-demand services and give customers instant gratification. From self-driving stores that the consumer can call to their location to drone-delivered parcels that arrive within an hour, both physical and online retailers have the opportunity to make their offerings hyper-convenient. ​</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" sz="1200" b="1" dirty="0"/><a:t>Streamline the path to purchase and point of sale. </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" sz="1200" dirty="0"/><a:t>Remove any element of inefficiency or inconvenience on the path to purchase and at the point of sale. At the point of sale, use automated services to remove the frustrations associated with waiting – or even the need for the checkout entirely. ​</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-GB" sz="1200" b="1" dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" sz="1200" b="1" dirty="0"/><a:t>Prepare stores for invisible commerce. </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-GB" sz="1200" dirty="0"/><a:t>As the point of sale becomes less visible, with customers being recognized through markers such as their phone or biometric identifiers, redesign brick-and-mortar spaces to match. What can you do with the floor space gained when checkouts are removed? Consider the losses too, such as fewer opportunities to catch customers' eyes while they wait to pay. Could push notifications that aid last-minute discovery complement your cashless store? Retailers in APAC, such as 7-Eleven and Alibaba, have already implemented multiple examples of invisible commerce, and Amazon Go is a flagship example in the US and UK. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:endParaRPr lang="en-GB" sz="1200" dirty="0"/></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:endParaRPr lang="en-GB" sz="1200" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="Slide Number Placeholder 5"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{9029E99B-B52A-558E-9C89-7EC102169